---
title: "Layout: a cell that will not stop"
---

Cell output is bounded in CSS: a runaway cell scrolls inside its own box instead of
taking the page's scrollbar hostage. Every shape below is deliberately kernel-free, so
this document renders identically with or without an interpreter.

The counts here are small on purpose. The bound is a CSS `max-height`, so what has to be
present is *overflow* (enough content to exceed the box), not a particular volume of it.
This document carried 400 stream lines and 200 table rows until 2026-08-09; the extra
bytes proved nothing the shapes below do not.

## A traceback that runs off the page {#sec-dense-pre}

